.TH DOOM\-BRIDGE 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded b06c570c" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
doom\-bridge \- Fenrir's Eye: read the Doom framebuffer and CPU state from pinned eBPF maps and stream frames to browsers over WebSocket.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B doom\-bridge
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fenrir's Eye: read the Doom framebuffer and CPU state from pinned eBPF maps and stream frames to browsers over WebSocket.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Run without BPF maps (serve fake gradient data)
.TP
.B \-\-map\-path \fISTRING\fR
BPF map pin directory (default /sys/fs/bpf/unheaded/doom\-ring/maps)
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIN\fR
WebSocket server port (default 16666)
.TP
.B \-\-static \fISTRING\fR
Static files directory (default: demos/doom/ relative to binary or CWD)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
doom\-bridge \-\-port 16666
doom\-bridge \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
